    "body": "Cause, proven by a test (branch `issue/3335-do-not-touch-pick`, worktree issue-917).\n\n**Reading 2 applies to 2D Offset and 3D Pocket.** These two kinds show the \"Pick protected\" button. The fault is in the click route:\n\n- The \"Click selects\" mode on the toolbar can be set to Models while the group shows \"Picking…\".\n- In Models mode, `interact::feature_routed` returns false. The viewport click goes to `pick_model` and selects the whole model. It does not go to `feature_click::click`, so the group gets no pick.\n- `feature_click::ask` already takes faces and edges for an armed Boundary row in every mode (#1727). Only the route did not agree with it.\n\nThe proof: the test `do_not_touch_takes_viewport_clicks_in_models_mode` (`crates/ui/src/egui_app/tests/do_not_touch_click.rs`) drives a real viewport click into the group of a 2D Offset. Before the fix it failed:\n\n```\nassertion `left == right` failed: a face click adds one row: [] / selected guard\n  left: 0\n right: 1\n```\n\nThe status \"selected guard\" shows that the click selected the model. In Edges mode the same click works (`do_not_touch_takes_a_face_and_an_edge_by_viewport_click` passed before the fix). The fix: `feature_routed` also returns true while a Boundary row is armed.\n\n**Reading 1 applies to all other kinds.**\n\n- Face, Contour, 2D Pocket, Adaptive2D, Finish3D, Trace and Engrave show the Boundary group. \"Do not touch\" shows only the refusal note, with no pick button (`do_not_touch_applies` in `crates/app/src/operation/types/avoid.rs`).\n- All other kinds (for example Drill, Slot, Probe) do not show the Boundary group. They show \"Boundary settings do not apply to it\".\n\nThis PR does not add support for more kinds. Generator support changes toolpaths and is under the safety floor. I file one sub-issue for each kind of the first list.\n",
    "author_association": "OWNER",
